If you choose handoff, open `docs/Handsoff.md` in the other AI tool first. The other tool must run `docs/Handsoff/bootstrap-sandbox.md` before implementing any slice; this is expected to create the bare Laravel scaffold in docs-only greenfield repos.

Where do you want to execute these slices?

  same-session  — this Claude Code session runs Phase 8 slice-by-slice
  subagents     — fresh subagents per slice, parallel where deps allow
  handoff       — stop here; you'll point another AI at docs/Handsoff.md

Recommendation: subagents
Why: keeps your conversation buffer clean while preserving Claude Code's tool access.
Tradeoffs: subagent failures are slightly harder to debug.

After choosing the venue, choose the review cadence:

  auto          — AI implements all slices or the entire app without stopping until the app is done and fully tested, unless a blocker/failing test requires user input
  manual-slice  — AI stops after every slice, prints the public sandbox URL, lists exactly what to test, waits for approval, then moves to the next slice
  manual-adr    — AI stops after each ADR/significant decision boundary with URL and tests before continuing
  manual-phase  — AI stops after major phases such as bootstrap, feature group, verification, and deployment prep

Recommendation: manual-slice for first builds; auto for trusted repeat runs after the plan is stable.
Why: manual-slice gives visible checkpoints while still allowing the AI to do the heavy implementation work.
Tradeoffs: auto is faster but delays user review until the full implementation or a failure.
